       (found on the real robot 2026-11-13). Each thigh/shin gets a
       collision-only convex hull of its mesh reduced to 32 vertices
       (*_hull meshes, group 3, no mass: bodies have explicit inertials);
       only left-vs-right pairs, so no same-leg excludes are needed. 32
       vertices: within 0-2.7 mm of the full hull, MJX ~15% slower (full
       meshes ~40%; bounding boxes touched ~5 mm early). Feet already collide
       with each other via their default contype. -->
